From 5146600548b569b9355d0bcedc71e5a55670b79a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:25:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): Heidenhain PECK and DEEP post the checked
 chain

The native G205 (Q258=0, full retract after each peck) and the peck
G200 (Q200=0) moved at FMAX to the cut face in the hole. The simulation
and the gouge check read the chain, which makes chip-break hops (PECK)
or rapids to R and feeds down from R (DEEP). The post now writes the
explicit chain for PECK and DEEP at each R clearance. DRILL and SPOT
keep G200 with Q202 = the whole depth. The Q208 machinery of G205 goes;
the Q395 level guard of G200 stays and is pinned.

Fixes #4224

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
